<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6300" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Callĭpŏlis</span></b> , is
			(acc. -im or -in), f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλλίπολις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Grecian city of Calabria</i>, now <i>Gallipoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town on the Thracian Chersonesus</i>, <i>opposite Lampsacus</i>, now <i>Gallipoli</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 31, 16, 6</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A town on the Tauric Chersonese</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 36,
				30, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
